{# Cookie notice - rendered while the `cookie_notice.enabled` setting is on
   (Admin -> Settings). It starts hidden, so the HTML stays the same for every
   visitor and cacheable; the inline script right after it shows it unless the
   visitor has already dismissed it. Not a dialog: it does not take focus or
   block the page.

   The notice is shown inline rather than from site/cookie-notice.ts because
   on a phone its text is often the largest block on screen, i.e. the
   Largest Contentful Paint element. Shown by the bundle it waited for every
   module to download and run (LCP 12-15 s against a 3.7 s first paint on
   hsgmagic.ru); shown here it is painted with the rest of the page.
   site/cookie-notice.ts still owns the offset, the button and the removal. #}
<section id="cookieNotice" class="{% block cookie_notice_class %}ui-cookie-notice{% endblock %}" aria-label="{{ trans('view.cookie_notice.label') }}" hidden>
    <div class="{% block cookie_notice_inner_class %}ui-container ui-cookie-notice__inner{% endblock %}">
        <p class="{% block cookie_notice_text_class %}ui-cookie-notice__text{% endblock %}">{{ trans('view.cookie_notice.text') }}</p>
        <button type="button" class="{% block cookie_notice_button_class %}ui-button ui-button--primary{% endblock %}" data-cookie-notice-accept>
            {{ trans('view.cookie_notice.accept') }}
        </button>
    </div>
</section>
<script>
    (() => {
        const notice = document.getElementById('cookieNotice');
        if (!notice || document.cookie.split(';').some(part => part.trim() === 'cookie_notice=1')) return;
        notice.hidden = false;
        document.documentElement.classList.add('has-cookie-notice');
    })();
</script>
